# Nami Trace product regression contract

Existing user-facing capabilities are permanent unless the user explicitly removes them.

Operational product surfaces:

- Overview
- Review Change
- Review Detail
- Impact Explorer
- Architecture
- Reports
- Report Detail
- Repository Health
- Research

Boundary Gate belongs to Review Change and Review Detail. It must never become Research-only functionality. Research is for evaluation, experiments, and aggregate validation metrics. It must not replace operational review workflows.

Reports are first-class product functionality. These remain supported:

- Change Intelligence Report
- Repository Intelligence Report
- Cluster / Workspace Intelligence Report
- PDF export
- Markdown export
- JSON export
- Evidence Package

Before completing any implementation:

- compare UI routes before and after
- compare API routes before and after
- verify report-generation actions remain visible
- verify export endpoints remain callable
- verify Review Change still executes Boundary Gate
- verify Review Detail still shows decision, evidence, actions, and validation
- verify Research remains evaluation-oriented
- run backend tests
- run the frontend production build
- run major demos

Refactoring does not authorize feature removal. A feature that still exists in backend code but becomes inaccessible through normal UI navigation counts as a regression.
